  "comment": "The product copy of the kernel (CoLabus): installed into host projects with docs/ops/kernel-install.cjs. managed is installed into every project and replaced on update; integration is merged into what the project already has; state is created only when absent. The host project owns AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md: the kernel adds one marker block to them. source and tests stay in this repository. workRoot is dropped because it names the development machine's drive: a host configures its own work root through PROTOCOL_WORK_ROOT or its own protocol-manifest.json. ruleGates is dropped because its derived-artifact rows name development tools: the product runs the rule gates on their code defaults, and a host writes its own ruleGates (budgets, demoted gates, allowed identities, derived artifacts) into its protocol-manifest.json, which an update keeps.",
